 =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)^{′}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{′}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)-(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡2x+2{sin}^{2}⁡2x \\\\  & =2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the Wronskian is not equal to zero, this confirms that the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are independent. \n\nLet's compute ${u}_{1}(x)$ and ${u}_{2}(x)$:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}(x) & =-\\int \\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {csc}^{2}⁡2x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2}(x) & =\\int \\frac{{csc}^{3}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{sin}^{3}⁡2x}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Then $du=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,dx,$ so $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,dx=\\frac{1}{2}\\,du,$ and the integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x}{{sin}^{3}⁡2x}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{3}}(\\frac{1}{2}\\,du) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int {u}^{-3}\\,du \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}{u}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8{sin}^{2}⁡2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}(x) & ={u}_{1}{y}_{1}+{u}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cot}⁡2x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+(-\\frac{1}{8{sin}^{2}⁡2x})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡2x}{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}-\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}(2{cos}^{2}⁡2x-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is the sum of the complementary and particular solutions, and can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,+\\,{{\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x.\n$$" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371626 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371627 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371628 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371629 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371630 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1041 "selection" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371629 13194139535872 true] [17592186371625 1110 #uuid "cffb04b3-0202-53e2-9cac-2592580f6980" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371626 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\operatorname{sec}⁡2x" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535872 true] [17592186371626 1111 #uuid "bd9029a9-fbd0-500a-a64e-34192a9548dd" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371627 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535872 true] [17592186371627 1111 #uuid "d72a261d-8fcd-594f-a08b-c2895688f990" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371628 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535872 true] [17592186371628 1111 #uuid "227c5b6f-0c99-58f0-a784-abc08f190577" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371629 1034 "\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\operatorname{csc}⁡2x" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535872 true] [17592186371629 1111 #uuid "80b444f0-2564-5163-aa4f-e5e8bb5c1ef0" 13194139535872 true] [17592186371630 1034 "\\frac{